{
  "_doc": "Scene-assembly recipes (plan section 7): intentional, locked anchors placed before any fill scatter. frame: 'face' = local +z points from 'anchor' toward 'face' (asset fronts face +z, see assets/nature/README.md), local +x = right of that; members with space 'world' use world x,z directly. yaw = degrees about +y added to the frame (positive = counter-clockwise seen from above). ground: 'min' = lowest terrain under the member's footprint (rocks emerge from slopes, never float), 'median' = median under footprint, 'center' = height at the origin, 'contact' (rocks) = highest no-float position (base touches the lowest terrain under the footprint). sink = extra metres lowered after grounding. fracture_yaw_jitter keeps one geological direction per outcrop: rock members get at most this much extra deterministic yaw. Members whose asset does not exist yet are skipped with a warning (reported in the manifest). reserve = fill scatter keeps trees/shrubs/rocks out of each member footprint grown by this margin (m). patches = flower/grass/fern density stamps added to the generated fields (radius m, strength 0..1).",
